Just in case anyone is wondering, I don't think a wand of wishing should
be camaflaged on its level by generating lots of other wands  ;^).

The only thing I can think of is a new magic "feature".  Wished-for wands,
scrolls, potions, rings, amulets, and spellbooks will, due to the perversity
of the magic that created them, appear to be another type of magic item, at
random.

This would only apply to the "neutrally generated" items, not items given
by a diety (although I don't think dieties currently give these items, do
they?).

For example, a wand of wishing might be randomly configured to appear
as a scroll of punishment.  You can pick the scroll up and it will go
into your "scrolls" inventory slot.  If you identify it then you will
discover its true identity.  Or, if you read the scroll, the wand will
get zapped.  All magic items would rotate through this random re-assignment
process.


